            <ArticleTitle>[Tuberous Sclerosis Complex Detected by Spontaneous Rupture of a Giant Renal Angiomyolipoma : A Case Report].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>111-114</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.14989/ActaUrolJap_63_3_111</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A woman in her 30s was admitted with abdominal pain and nausea. CT scan revealed a spontaneous rupture of the right giant renal angiomyolipoma, and trans-arterial embolization was performed successfully. With further examination, she was found to be affected with tuberous sclerosis complex (TSC) and she finally wastreated with everolimusfor prevention of recurrent spontaneous-rupture of renal angiomyolipoma.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
